{"reference":"1 Kings 1","book":"1 Kings","chapter":1,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"chapter_overview","title":"Overview","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"First Kings opens with a contested succession: as David’s strength fails, Adonijah tries to establish himself as king, while David publicly appoints and anoints Solomon. This beginning sets the book’s larger movement from Solomon’s reign—its wisdom, temple, and later failure—to divided kingdoms and prophetic confrontation under Ahab.","verse_refs":["1 Kings 1:1-53"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_kings_001_3fb922959429060c1063eda9"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}